From: AKADATA LIMITED <linux@saphira.vm2.uk>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:07:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] ccram: params, pick and normal-min floor framework
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Part of CCRAM — AKADATA LIMITED adaptation of Meta CRAM.  CCRAM is
based on Meta's CRAM work (Gregory Price; see CRAM.PROVENANCE in
linux-saphira-meta-cram) and extends/adapts it for Saphira Linux.
Meta's CRAM mechanism is used as-is; this series is Saphira-original
integration code.  Licence: GPL-2.0-only.

This patch: Kconfig option, build glue, entry-point declarations,
ccram=/ccram.normal_min= parsing, top-down reservation-aware range
pick with the hard normal-RAM floor, and the fail-closed reason
framework.  No callers yet; excision, validation and registration
follow as separate patches.
---
 include/linux/ccram_sysram.h |  15 ++++
 mm/Kconfig                   |  14 +++
 mm/Makefile                  |   1 +
 mm/ccram_sysram.c            | 159 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 189 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/linux/ccram_sysram.h
 create mode 100644 mm/ccram_sysram.c

